The` ldrb` instruction shouldn’t be hogging CPU! How do we reproduce this?


Unfortunately, the Network Extension fork creation handler registration code is a bit hard to reproduce, but this` _os_log_preferences_refresh` path seems pretty pervasive in their Network Extension code. In fact,[there is a similar bug report](https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/834537) that hit the same leaf instruction of` _os_log_preferences_refresh` . Thankfully, it seems like this dylib isn’t changing very much across macOS versions! Although the reproduction case does not rely on the same fork creation handlers in our original` sample` trace, let’s check if the segfault is on the same instruction. The segfault was a bit flaky, so we added a loop here:


